Subject: [PATCH] simoop: Use a spin-wait hint that builds on arm64

usec_spin() hints the CPU with "rep;nop", which is x86's PAUSE and
does not assemble anywhere else, so simoop fails to build on arm64.
Keep it on x86, use "yield" on arm64 (as the kernel's cpu_relax()
does) and only a compiler barrier elsewhere. The loop still stops on
wall time, so how long it spins is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/simoop.c b/simoop.c
index 6410ab6..e706d75 100644
--- a/simoop.c
+++ b/simoop.c
@@ -884,7 +884,13 @@ struct thread_data {
 	struct stats stats[TOTAL_STATS];
 };
 
+#if defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__)
 #define nop __asm__ __volatile__("rep;nop": : :"memory")
+#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+#define nop __asm__ __volatile__("yield": : :"memory")
+#else
+#define nop __asm__ __volatile__("": : :"memory")
+#endif
 static void usec_spin(unsigned long spin_time)
 {
 	struct timeval now;
